1	1	"[[\\"Whole Milk\\",360],[\\"Heavy Cream\\",360],[\\"Skimmed Milk Powder\\",55],[\\"Egg Yolk\\",36],[\\"Sucrose\\",70],[\\"Dextrose\\",25],[\\"Invert Sugar\\",15],[\\"Locust Bean Gum\\",0.8],[\\"Guar Gum\\",0.4],[\\"Lambda Carrageenan\\",0.2],[\\"Salt\\",0.7]]"	[Underbelly's Standard Base](https://under-belly.org/basic-ice-cream-recipe-examples/) recipe,\nposted 2016-05-25, visited 2026-05-7.\n\n'Whole Milk' is quoted as 3.3%, which I assume is 3.25% rounded up, consistent with Sci-Cream's\ndefinition. 'Heavy Cream' is quoted as 36%, consistent with Sci-Cream's definition. The 'Egg Yolk'\namount is a whole multiple of 18g large egg yolks. The stabilizers are the 4:2:1 'Underbelly General\nPurpose Stabilizer Blend', total 1.4g.\n\nThe 15g of 'Invert Sugar' can be replaced by 6g each of 'Dextrose' and 'Fructose', as per\n[this](https://under-belly.org/basic-ice-cream-recipe-examples/#comment-709) and\n[this](https://under-belly.org/basic-ice-cream-recipe-examples/#comment-12) comment, which is much\neasier to work with.	\N	\N	\N	2026-11-23 01:49:33.668201	\N
2	1	"[[\\"Whole Milk\\",360],[\\"Heavy Cream\\",360],[\\"Skimmed Milk Powder\\",15],[\\"Egg Yolk\\",108],[\\"Sucrose\\",75],[\\"Dextrose\\",35],[\\"Invert Sugar\\",15],[\\"Locust Bean Gum\\",0.6],[\\"Guar Gum\\",0.3],[\\"Lambda Carrageenan\\",0.15],[\\"Salt\\",0.7]]"	[Underbelly's French Variation](https://under-belly.org/basic-ice-cream-recipe-examples/) recipe,\nposted 2016-05-25, visited 2026-05-7.\n\n'Whole Milk' is quoted as 3.3%, which I assume is 3.25% rounded up, consistent with Sci-Cream's\ndefinition. 'Heavy Cream' is quoted as 36%, consistent with Sci-Cream's definition. The 'Egg Yolk'\namount is a whole multiple of 18g large egg yolks. The stabilizers are the 4:2:1 'Underbelly General\nPurpose Stabilizer Blend', total 1.05g.\n\nThe 15g of 'Invert Sugar' can be replaced by 6g each of 'Dextrose' and 'Fructose', as per\n[this](https://under-belly.org/basic-ice-cream-recipe-examples/#comment-709) and\n[this](https://under-belly.org/basic-ice-cream-recipe-examples/#comment-12) comment, which is much\neasier to work with.	\N	\N	\N	2026-11-23 01:49:33.671172	\N
3	1	"[[\\"Whole Milk\\",480],[\\"Heavy Cream\\",240],[\\"Skimmed Milk Powder\\",85],[\\"Sucrose\\",70],[\\"Dextrose\\",30],[\\"Invert Sugar\\",15],[\\"Soy Lecithin Powder\\",2],[\\"Locust Bean Gum\\",0.8],[\\"Guar Gum\\",0.6],[\\"Lambda Carrageenan\\",0.4],[\\"Salt\\",0.7]]"	[Underbelly's Light Variation](https://under-belly.org/basic-ice-cream-recipe-examples/) recipe,\nposted 2016-05-25, visited 2026-05-7.\n\n'Whole Milk' is quoted as 3.3%, which I assume is 3.25% rounded up, consistent with Sci-Cream's\ndefinition. 'Heavy Cream' is quoted as 36%, consistent with Sci-Cream's definition. The stabilizers\nare a 4:3:2 blend, total 1.8g, and 2g of 'Soy Lecithin'. This is inconsistent with 'Underbelly\nEggless Ice Cream Stabilizer Blend', which uses a 4:2:1 blend, and 4 'Soy Lecithin'. It's also\ninconsistent with the 2.1g of stabilizers in the composition table, and with the stated 4.5g of 'Soy\nLecithin' in the discussion. The stabilizer blends were both ostensibly edited on 2018-10, but they\nare inconsistent with each other.\n\nThe 15g of 'Invert Sugar' can be replaced by 6g each of 'Dextrose' and 'Fructose', as per\n[this](https://under-belly.org/basic-ice-cream-recipe-examples/#comment-709) and\n[this](https://under-belly.org/basic-ice-cream-recipe-examples/#comment-12) comment, which is much\neasier to work with.	\N	\N	\N	2026-11-23 01:49:33.673646	\N
4	1	"[[\\"Whole Milk\\",470],[\\"Heavy Cream\\",240],[\\"Cocoa Powder, 22% Fat\\",70],[\\"70% Dark Chocolate\\",90],[\\"Dextrose\\",84],[\\"Fructose\\",29],[\\"Soy Lecithin Powder\\",2],[\\"Locust Bean Gum\\",0.8],[\\"Guar Gum\\",0.6],[\\"Lambda Carrageenan\\",0.4],[\\"Salt\\",1.2],[\\"Vanilla Extract\\",10]]"	[Underbelly's "Double Origin" Chocolate Ice\nCream](https://under-belly.org/ice-cream-flavor-chocolate/) recipe, posted 2018-09-25, visited\n2026-06-16.\n\nCocoa powder is assumed to be 22% fat, typical of the brands mentioned, e.g. Valrhona, and agrees\nwith the stated total fat content. Chocolate is assumed to be 70% dark chocolate, in the middle of\nthe stated 67-72% range. The stabilizers are a 4:3:2 blend, total 1.8g, and 2g of 'Soy Lecithin' -\nthis does not match any of Underbelly's listed stabilizer blends, though it does match the 'Light\nVariation' blend. The resulting composition agrees with the stated 'Analysis' - except POD and PAC.	\N	\N	\N	2026-11-23 01:49:33.676068	\N
