USDA Milk Chocolate	1	Chocolate	"{\\"name\\":\\"USDA Milk Chocolate\\",\\"category\\":\\"Chocolate\\",\\"ChocolateSpec\\":{\\"cacao_solids\\":33.5,\\"milk_solids\\":20,\\"total_fat\\":29.7,\\"sugars\\":43.4,\\"other_solids\\":3.1},\\"comments\\":\\"USDA FoodData Central - SR Legacy - [Candies, milk\\\\nchocolate](https://fdc.nal.usda.gov/food-details/167587/nutrients)\\\\n\\\\nThe dark chocolate entries take `cacao_solids` as `100 - sugars`, but this listing also contains\\\\nmilk solids, which need to be estimated. This SR Legacy listing does not report lactose, so the\\\\nsplit between cocoa and milk is instead derived from the reported fiber and protein; see\\\\n[`estimate_chocolate_snf_split_from_protein_by_fiber`](https://docs.rs/sci-cream/latest/sci_cream/specs/chocolate/util/fn.estimate_chocolate_snf_split_from_protein_by_fiber.html).\\\\n\\\\n- `cacao_solids` as `total_fat - milk_fat` plus cocoa solids non-fat, via\\\\n  [`estimate_chocolate_cocoa_snf_from_fiber`](https://docs.rs/sci-cream/latest/sci_cream/specs/chocolate/util/fn.estimate_chocolate_cocoa_snf_from_fiber.html) and the 3.4 g of fiber. `milk_fat` is\\\\n  <code>milk_solids \\\\\\\\* [STD_BUTTERFAT_IN_WHOLE_MILK_POWDER]</code>\\\\n- `milk_solids` as <code>MSNF / (1 - [STD_BUTTERFAT_IN_WHOLE_MILK_POWDER])</code>, where\\\\n  MSNF is estimated as 14.8% via [`estimate_chocolate_snf_split_from_protein_by_fiber`](https://docs.rs/sci-cream/latest/sci_cream/specs/chocolate/util/fn.estimate_chocolate_snf_split_from_protein_by_fiber.html) and the\\\\n  7.65 g of protein and 3.4 g of fiber\\\\n- `total_fat` from the listing, internally split into cocoa butter and milk fat by [`ChocolateSpec`](https://docs.rs/sci-cream/latest/sci_cream/specs/chocolate/chocolate/struct.ChocolateSpec.html)\\\\n- `sugars` as the 51.5 g total less the lactose that MSNF carries, at [`STD_LACTOSE_IN_MSNF`](https://docs.rs/sci-cream/latest/sci_cream/constants/composition/dairy/milk/constant.STD_LACTOSE_IN_MSNF.html)\\\\n- `other_solids` as the remainder, the listing's 1.5% water and 1.6% more, such as emulsifier\\"}"
USDA White Chocolate	1	Chocolate	"{\\"name\\":\\"USDA White Chocolate\\",\\"category\\":\\"Chocolate\\",\\"ChocolateSpec\\":{\\"cacao_solids\\":27.2,\\"milk_solids\\":20.7,\\"total_fat\\":32.1,\\"sugars\\":50.7,\\"other_solids\\":1.4},\\"comments\\":\\"USDA FoodData Central - SR Legacy - [Candies, white\\\\nchocolate](https://fdc.nal.usda.gov/food-details/167571/nutrients)\\\\n\\\\nThe dark chocolate entries take `cacao_solids` as `100 - sugars`, but this listing also contains\\\\nmilk solids, which need to be estimated. This SR Legacy listing does not report lactose, so the\\\\nsplit between cocoa and milk is instead derived from the reported fiber and protein; see\\\\n[`estimate_chocolate_snf_split_from_protein_by_fiber`](https://docs.rs/sci-cream/latest/sci_cream/specs/chocolate/util/fn.estimate_chocolate_snf_split_from_protein_by_fiber.html).\\\\n\\\\nThe listing's 0.2 g of fiber puts the cocoa solids non-fat at 0.5%, so nearly all the cacao solids\\\\nare cocoa butter, and nearly all the protein is milk's, as expected of white chocolate.\\\\n\\\\n- `cacao_solids` as `total_fat - milk_fat` plus cocoa solids non-fat, via\\\\n  [`estimate_chocolate_cocoa_snf_from_fiber`](https://docs.rs/sci-cream/latest/sci_cream/specs/chocolate/util/fn.estimate_chocolate_cocoa_snf_from_fiber.html) and the 0.2 g of fiber. `milk_fat` is\\\\n  <code>milk_solids \\\\\\\\* [STD_BUTTERFAT_IN_WHOLE_MILK_POWDER]</code>\\\\n- `milk_solids` as <code>MSNF / (1 - [STD_BUTTERFAT_IN_WHOLE_MILK_POWDER])</code>, where\\\\n  MSNF is estimated as 15.3% via [`estimate_chocolate_snf_split_from_protein_by_fiber`](https://docs.rs/sci-cream/latest/sci_cream/specs/chocolate/util/fn.estimate_chocolate_snf_split_from_protein_by_fiber.html) and the\\\\n  5.87 g of protein and 0.2 g of fiber\\\\n- `total_fat` from the listing, internally split into cocoa butter and milk fat by [`ChocolateSpec`](https://docs.rs/sci-cream/latest/sci_cream/specs/chocolate/chocolate/struct.ChocolateSpec.html)\\\\n- `sugars` as the 59.0 g total less the lactose that MSNF carries, at [`STD_LACTOSE_IN_MSNF`](https://docs.rs/sci-cream/latest/sci_cream/constants/composition/dairy/milk/constant.STD_LACTOSE_IN_MSNF.html)\\\\n- `other_solids` as the remainder, the listing's 1.3% water and 0.1% more, such as emulsifier\\"}"
