Liquid Soy Lecithin	1	Emulsifier	"{\\"name\\":\\"Liquid Soy Lecithin\\",\\"category\\":\\"Emulsifier\\",\\"EmulsifierSpec\\":{\\"emulsifiers\\":{\\"lecithin\\":60},\\"other_solids\\":{\\"fats\\":{\\"total\\":40}}},\\"comments\\":\\"Liquid soy lecithin with a minimum purity (acetone insoluble substances) of ~60%; the remaining\\\\nsubstances are mostly triglycerides (The European Commission, 2025, E322)[^10], (East Harbour Group,\\\\n2026, \\\\\\"Lecithin, Technical Specification\\\\\\")[^522], (Konsonet, 2026, \\\\\\"Soya Lecithin Liquid\\\\nGMO\\\\\\")[^523], (EFSA et al., 2017, 3.1.1 Identity of the substance)[^75].\\\\n\\\\n[^10]: The European Commission. (2025). [_Commission Regulation (EU) No 231/2012_](https://eur-lex.europa.eu/eli/reg/2012/231/oj).\\\\n[^75]: EFSA Panel on Food Additives and Nutrient Sources added to Food (ANS), et al. (2017, April). [_Re-evaluation of lecithins (E 322) as a food additive_](https://doi.org/10.2903/j.efsa.2017.4742). EFSA Journal, 15(4), e04742.\\\\n[^522]: [_Lecithin, Technical Specification TDS-145-V2_](https://www.eastharbourgroup.com/storage/download-files/lecithin/Lecithin-TDS-145-V2.pdf). (2026). East Harbour Group.\\\\n[^523]: [_Soya Lecithin Liquid GMO - SLLGM-60_](https://konsonet.eu/wp-content/uploads/2024/05/specifications-soya-lecithin-liquid-SLLGM-60-gmo-Konsonet.pdf). (2026). Konsonet.\\"}"
Sunflower Lecithin Powder	1	Emulsifier	"{\\"name\\":\\"Sunflower Lecithin Powder\\",\\"category\\":\\"Emulsifier\\",\\"EmulsifierSpec\\":{\\"emulsifiers\\":{\\"lecithin\\":95},\\"other_solids\\":{\\"fats\\":{\\"total\\":5}}},\\"comments\\":\\"De-oiled sunflower lecithin powder with a purity (acetone insoluble substances) of ~95%; the\\\\nremaining substances are mostly triglycerides (EFSA et al., 2017, 3.1.1 Identity of the\\\\nsubstance)[^75].\\\\n\\\\n[^75]: EFSA Panel on Food Additives and Nutrient Sources added to Food (ANS), et al. (2017, April). [_Re-evaluation of lecithins (E 322) as a food additive_](https://doi.org/10.2903/j.efsa.2017.4742). EFSA Journal, 15(4), e04742.\\"}"
Liquid Sunflower Lecithin	1	Emulsifier	"{\\"name\\":\\"Liquid Sunflower Lecithin\\",\\"category\\":\\"Emulsifier\\",\\"EmulsifierSpec\\":{\\"emulsifiers\\":{\\"lecithin\\":60},\\"other_solids\\":{\\"fats\\":{\\"total\\":40}}},\\"comments\\":\\"Liquid sunflower lecithin with a minimum purity (acetone insoluble substances) of ~60%; the\\\\nremaining substances are mostly triglycerides (The European Commission, 2025, E322)[^10], (EFSA et\\\\nal., 2017, 3.1.1 Identity of the substance)[^75]; its phospholipid composition is comparable to that\\\\nof liquid soy lecithin (EFSA et al., 2017, Table 2)[^75].\\\\n\\\\n[^10]: The European Commission. (2025). [_Commission Regulation (EU) No 231/2012_](https://eur-lex.europa.eu/eli/reg/2012/231/oj).\\\\n[^75]: EFSA Panel on Food Additives and Nutrient Sources added to Food (ANS), et al. (2017, April). [_Re-evaluation of lecithins (E 322) as a food additive_](https://doi.org/10.2903/j.efsa.2017.4742). EFSA Journal, 15(4), e04742.\\"}"
Egg Yolk Lecithin	1	Emulsifier	"{\\"name\\":\\"Egg Yolk Lecithin\\",\\"category\\":\\"Emulsifier\\",\\"EmulsifierSpec\\":{\\"emulsifiers\\":{\\"lecithin\\":100}}}"
Gum Arabic	1	Emulsifier	"{\\"name\\":\\"Gum Arabic\\",\\"category\\":\\"Emulsifier\\",\\"EmulsifierSpec\\":{\\"emulsifiers\\":{\\"gum_arabic\\":100}},\\"comments\\":\\"By EU regulation, gum arabic (E414) products can have up to 17% water and 4% ash (The European\\\\nCommission, 2025, E414)[^10]. Here it is modeled as 100% `gum_arabic` since \\\\\\"gum arabic\\\\\\" products\\\\naren't sold at a range of purity grades, and aside from emulsification the solids composition has no\\\\nmeaningful effect in the ice cream formulation at normal usage levels.\\\\n\\\\n[^10]: The European Commission. (2025). [_Commission Regulation (EU) No 231/2012_](https://eur-lex.europa.eu/eli/reg/2012/231/oj).\\"}"
Mono- and Diglycerides	1	Emulsifier	"{\\"name\\":\\"Mono- and Diglycerides\\",\\"category\\":\\"Emulsifier\\",\\"EmulsifierSpec\\":{\\"emulsifiers\\":{\\"mono_and_diglycerides\\":100}}}"
Distilled Monoglycerides	1	Emulsifier	"{\\"name\\":\\"Distilled Monoglycerides\\",\\"category\\":\\"Emulsifier\\",\\"EmulsifierSpec\\":{\\"emulsifiers\\":{\\"distilled_monoglycerides\\":100}},\\"comments\\":\\"High-purity distilled monoglycerides (DMG) - such as glycerol monostearate or glycerol monooleate,\\\\nabove 90% monoglycerides, produced via molecular distillation under vacuum of the standard 40-55%\\\\ngrade (Food Ingredients Asia, 2026)[^80]. See 'Glycerol Monostearate' for the standard grade, which\\\\nis sold under the same E471 designation.\\\\n\\\\n[^80]: [_Glycerol Monostearate_](https://www.foodingredientsasia.com/en/learning-center/product-based-knowledge/glycerol-monostearate). (n.d.). Food Ingredients Asia. Retrieved 2026, September.\\"}"
Polysorbate 80	1	Emulsifier	"{\\"name\\":\\"Polysorbate 80\\",\\"category\\":\\"Emulsifier\\",\\"EmulsifierSpec\\":{\\"emulsifiers\\":{\\"polysorbate_80\\":100}},\\"comments\\":\\"This library does not support modelling the compounds in Polysorbate 80. However, it is used in such\\\\nminute quantities - at most 0.1% of the finished frozen dessert (U.S. FDA, CFR 21, 172.840)[^52] -\\\\nthat its composition is negligible in formulations. As such, it is deliberately not tracked here,\\\\nmodeled as unclassified solids; they are a closer approximation than water, since the compounds are\\\\nnon-volatile.\\\\n\\\\n[^52]: U.S. Food & Drug Administration. (n.d.). [_CFR - Code of Federal Regulations Title 21_](https://www.ecfr.gov/current/title-21).\\"}"
Glycerol Monostearate	1	Emulsifier	"{\\"name\\":\\"Glycerol Monostearate\\",\\"category\\":\\"Emulsifier\\",\\"EmulsifierSpec\\":{\\"emulsifiers\\":{\\"mono_and_diglycerides\\":100}},\\"comments\\":\\"Glycerol monostearate (GMS) is available in standard grades (40-55% monoglycerides content) and\\\\ndistilled grades (above 90% monoglycerides content), also referred to as 'Distilled Monoglycerides'\\\\nor DMG; both are sold under the same E471 designation (Food Ingredients Asia, 2026)[^80]. This entry\\\\nis the standard grade (British Pharmacopoeia Commission, 2013)[^78]; see 'Distilled Monoglycerides'\\\\nfor the high-purity above 90% grade. Note that USP-NF reserves _Glyceryl Monostearate_ for the >90%\\\\ngrade (United States Pharmacopeia)[^79].\\\\n\\\\n[^78]: British Pharmacopoeia Commission. (2013). [_Glycerol Monostearate 40-55_](https://www.drugfuture.com/Pharmacopoeia/BP2013/data/7561.html). British Pharmacopoeia, Ph. Eur. monograph 0495.\\\\n[^79]: United States Pharmacopeia. (n.d.). [_Glyceryl Monostearate_](https://doi.usp.org/USPNF/USPNF_M35490_03_01.html). USP-NF. Retrieved 2026, September.\\\\n[^80]: [_Glycerol Monostearate_](https://www.foodingredientsasia.com/en/learning-center/product-based-knowledge/glycerol-monostearate). (n.d.). Food Ingredients Asia. Retrieved 2026, September.\\"}"
