Pectin	1	Stabilizer	"{\\"name\\":\\"Pectin\\",\\"category\\":\\"Stabilizer\\",\\"StabilizerSpec\\":{\\"stabilizers\\":{\\"pectin\\":100}},\\"comments\\":\\"This models pure pectin E440, which requires a minimum of 65% galacturonic acid on the ash-free and\\\\nanhydrous basis, and allows up to 12% water (The European Commission, 2025, E440)[^10]. Unlike the\\\\nother entries of individual stabilizers, it does _not_ model most retail pectin products, which\\\\ntypically include fillers like dextrose, often at higher proportions than the active pectin (Kraft\\\\nHeinz, 2026, \\\\\\"Sure-Jell\\\\\\")[^524]. Those should be modeled via [`CompositeSpec`](https://docs.rs/sci-cream/latest/sci_cream/specs/composite/struct.CompositeSpec.html) including pure pectin\\\\nand fillers as separate ingredients.\\\\n\\\\n[^10]: The European Commission. (2025). [_Commission Regulation (EU) No 231/2012_](https://eur-lex.europa.eu/eli/reg/2012/231/oj).\\\\n[^524]: [_Sure-Jell Original Premium Fruit Pectin_](https://www.kraftheinz.com/sure-jell/products/00043000293201-original-premium-fruit-pectin). (2026). Kraft Heinz.\\"}"
